<title>POLAND: Poland C/A deficit $358 mln in September. [CORRECTED 16:40 GMT]</title>
<headline>Poland C/A deficit $358 mln in September. [CORRECTED 16:40 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland had a current account deficit of $358 million in September bringing the shortfall in the January-September period to $311 million, the National Bank of Poland said.  </p>
<p> POLISH CURRENT ACCOUNT	   SEP 1996    AUG 1996   SEP 1995</p>
<p> current account million USD	-358		58	 -281</p>
<p> merchandise trade balance	  -764	    -810	 -217</p>
<p> exports				 2,011	   1,906	1,898</p>
<p> imports				 2,775	   2,716	2,115</p>
<p> unclassified flows balance	  619	     703	  NA @</p>
<p>					 JAN-SEP 1996  JAN-SEP 1995</p>
<p> current account million USD	-311	   4,167</p>
<p>(Corrects current account figure for Jan-Sep 1995 from -1,382)</p>
<p> merchandise trade balance	-5,260	    -930</p>
<p> exports				17,632	  16,634</p>
<p> imports				22,892	  17,564</p>
<p> unclassified flows balance	5,517	     NA</p>
<p>Note. From January 1996 the central bank introduced a new category, &quot;unclassified flows&quot; which encompasses mainly cross-border, unregistered trade flows.</p>
<p>Jan-September 1995 trade figures were adjusted to make them comparable with 1996 data. No adjusted figures were given for September 1995.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
